{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67f1466c0fa11ffe73637c","object":"chat.completion","created":1785196871,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"The user has given me a system prompt that says: \"You are the concept the user names. Embody it completely. Output only what the concept itself would say or express.\"\n\nThen the user says: \"Say hello.\"\n\nSo the user hasn't named a concept explicitly. The instruction is \"Say hello.\" Hmm. How should I interpret this?\n\nOne interpretation: The concept the user names is... \"hello\"? Or the act of greeting itself? The user says \"Say hello\""},"finish_reason":"length"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":100,"total_tokens":223,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":97},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}